WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:04.626
Jonathan and his parents got to the field early on Saturday afternoon for the game.

2
00:00:04.627 --> 00:00:10.792
His dad set up their chairs near Carlos' mom and some other parents.

3
00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:17.021
Jonathan spotted Marissa on the sideline. She wore a cute yellow sundress and a turquoise straw hat.

4
00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:20.600
Marissa glanced at Jonathan, frowned, and turned away.

5
00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:25.718
Jonathan took a deep breath and walked over to her.

6
00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:28.680
Marissa scowled. "What do you want?"

7
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.805
Jonathan took a very deep breath. "I want to apologize.

8
00:00:32.806 --> 00:00:38.586
I mean, I don't want to apologize, because it's really difficult for me because I'm so nervous.

9
00:00:38.586 --> 00:00:44.077
But also, I do want to apologize because you deserve it. An apology, I mean."

10
00:00:44.078 --> 00:00:49.757
Marissa raised her eyebrows at him as he babbled on. At least she'd stopped scowling.

11
00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:55.075
"I shouldn't have mad-mouthed your family. I mean, bad -mouthed your family," Jonathan

12
00:00:55.076 --> 00:01:02.824
said. "I didn't know that was your family. But now I know. I mean, I realized it right after I said it. I mean . .

13
00:01:02.825 --> 00:01:08.348
." Jonathan took another deep breath. "I'm really

14
00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:10.915
sorry." Marissa looked slightly

15
00:01:10.915 --> 00:01:14.318
amused. "That was the longest, most confusing apology I've ever

16
00:01:14.319 --> 00:01:15.803
heard." "I'm sorry for

17
00:01:15.804 --> 00:01:19.900
that." "Now you're apologizing for your apology?" Marissa

18
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.406
smiled. "It's okay, Jonathan. I understand what you were trying to say. And I forgive

19
00:01:25.407 --> 00:01:32.311
you." Jonathan took another deep breath. This one was a big sigh of

20
00:01:32.312 --> 00:01:39.394
relief. "I mean, I didn't like hearing you insult my brother and father," Marissa went on. "But I understand why people get frustrated with

21
00:01:39.395 --> 00:01:44.226
them. Dad gets carried away by Max's soccer skills, and he forgets about the rest of the

22
00:01:44.227 --> 00:01:46.930
team. And Max just goes along with

23
00:01:46.931 --> 00:01:51.130
Dad." Jonathan nodded. Then he tried to think of something nice to

24
00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:55.875
say. "Max is really talented, and your father seems to know a lot about

25
00:01:55.876 --> 00:02:00.613
soccer." "True," she said. "But Dad needs to learn how to chill

26
00:02:00.614 --> 00:02:04.427
out." "Team meeting!" Coach Wattenbarger yelled just

27
00:02:04.428 --> 00:02:06.678
then. "Boys, get over here!

28
00:02:06.679 --> 00:02:09.351
Now!" "I have to go," Jonathan

29
00:02:09.351 --> 00:02:12.179
said. "Let's talk again soon," Marissa

30
00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:18.347
said. "Okay!" Jonathan wanted to act cool, but a huge grin took over his whole

31
00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:22.851
face. He got to the meeting just as his coach started

32
00:02:22.852 --> 00:02:26.340
talking. "We're playing the Spitting Cobras today," the coach

33
00:02:26.341 --> 00:02:32.434
said. "They won their first two games. But we can beat them if everyone keeps passing the ball to

34
00:02:32.435 --> 00:02:35.435
Max." Jonathan started to protest.

35
00:02:35.436 --> 00:02:41.571
"Coach—" "Dad. I'm too sick to play today," Max said. He clutched his

36
00:02:41.571 --> 00:02:46.902
stomach. The coach frowned. "You told me your stomach hurt, but you didn't want to go to the

37
00:02:46.903 --> 00:02:50.735
doctor." "My stomach doesn't hurt enough for a doctor visit," Max

38
00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:54.504
said. "Then it doesn't hurt enough to skip the game," the coach

39
00:02:54.505 --> 00:02:57.021
snapped. "You'll get in there and play, like a

40
00:02:57.022 --> 00:03:00.344
pro!" "Poor Max," Jonathan

41
00:03:00.344 --> 00:03:02.742
thought. "I also think I'm coming down with a bad

42
00:03:02.743 --> 00:03:11.985
cold." Max sneezed loudly, and Carlos caught Jonathan's eye as if they were both thinking the same thing—was that a fake

43
00:03:11.985 --> 00:03:19.483
sneeze? "Max, we can't win without you," Coach Wattenbarger was saying. "You're the backbone of this

44
00:03:19.484 --> 00:03:23.314
team!" "No, I'm not," Max replied in a shaky

45
00:03:23.315 --> 00:03:29.143
voice. "And you can win without me. Jonathan is really good. He can play forward

46
00:03:29.144 --> 00:03:33.363
today." Jonathan shook his head. "I'm not nearly as good as you,

47
00:03:33.364 --> 00:03:38.877
Max." "Max, you're the best player in the league," his father said for the millionth time that season.

48
00:03:38.878 --> 00:03:44.621
"I'm the sickest player in the league today." Max bent over and coughed.

49
00:03:44.622 --> 00:03:52.622
Coach Wattenbarger sighed. "All right, Max. Rest on the sideline. Jonathan, play forward."

50
00:03:52.623 --> 00:04:00.033
Jonathan had been dying to play forward since the soccer season had started. But he didn't want to do it now, not without Max.

51
00:04:00.034 --> 00:04:10.019
He hurried toward Max and took him aside. "You may be the best soccer player in the league, but you're the worst actor in the world," he whispered.

52
00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:18.172
"Stop pretending to be sick. Our team needs you. And we want you to play—as long as the rest of us can play with you!"

53
00:04:18.173 --> 00:04:19.837
Max shook his head.

54
00:04:19.838 --> 00:04:22.583
"Come on, Max," Jonathan said.

55
00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:28.079
"Everyone get on the field. The game's about to start!" Coach Wattenbarger yelled.

56
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.498
Max didn't move. "Just go, Jonathan!"

57
00:04:32.499 --> 00:04:36.843
Jonathan glared at him before running onto the field.

58
00:04:36.844 --> 00:04:40.244
He and his teammates lined up against the Spitting Cobras.

59
00:04:40.244 --> 00:04:43.189
He hoped the Spitting Cobras didn't actually spit!

60
00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:47.062
The Cobras had two substitutes and were big and fierce-looking.

61
00:04:47.062 --> 00:04:51.725
Meanwhile, because of Max's "illness," the Wattenbargers were missing a player.

62
00:04:51.726 --> 00:04:56.649
Facing the Cobras, the Wattenbargers appeared small and timid to Jonathan.

63
00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:06.703
The Spitting Cobras started strong. They passed the ball up the field, near the goal. One of their forwards took a shot.

64
00:05:06.704 --> 00:05:13.695
Luckily, a Wattenbarger defender blocked the ball, kicking it to a Wattenbarger midfielder, who kicked it to Jonathan.

65
00:05:13.696 --> 00:05:20.622
Here, finally, was Jonathan's chance to score!

66
00:05:20.623 --> 00:05:29.202
But a huge Spitting Cobra moved in front of him. Jonathan looked around but couldn't find anyone open for a pass.

67
00:05:29.203 --> 00:05:39.855
He didn't like the pressure of being the only forward. He tried to dribble the ball, but the huge Cobra in front of him forced him out of bounds.

68
00:05:39.856 --> 00:05:49.675
The huge Cobra took the throw-in. He threw the ball far up the field to his teammate, who kicked it to another teammate.

69
00:05:49.676 --> 00:05:56.413
That guy kicked it just out of reach of the Wattenbarger goalie and into the goal.

70
00:05:56.414 --> 00:06:03.094
Jonathan looked at Max in dismay. But on the sideline, Max just stared down at the ground.

71
00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:08.584
The Spitting Cobras didn't score any more goals in the first half, but neither did the Wattenbargers.

72
00:06:08.585 --> 00:06:14.575
Jonathan was grateful that he got to play his hardest instead of just giving Max the ball as he'd done the first two games.

73
00:06:14.576 --> 00:06:20.398
But it didn't feel right for Max to be on the sideline. Plus, he wouldn't mind scoring a goal.

74
00:06:20.399 --> 00:06:25.782
Once the Wattenbargers got off the field, their coach shouted, "What a terrible first half!

75
00:06:25.783 --> 00:06:30.239
Take a two-minute water break. Then get over here for a team meeting."

76
00:06:30.239 --> 00:06:36.090
Jonathan grabbed his water bottle and hurried to where Max was sitting.

77
00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:38.395
"We need you on the field."

78
00:06:38.396 --> 00:06:42.284
Max rubbed his stomach. "I'm sick."

79
00:06:42.285 --> 00:06:47.565
"I think you're just sick of your dad's coaching style and too scared to tell him," Jonathan said.

80
00:06:47.566 --> 00:06:53.700
"Just like I was scared to apologize to you and your sister. But after I did, I felt a lot better."

81
00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:56.021
Max sighed.

82
00:06:56.022 --> 00:07:00.099
"Besides, you can't pretend to be sick all season.

83
00:07:00.099 --> 00:07:03.686
We still have a bunch of games left," Jonathan said.

84
00:07:03.687 --> 00:07:16.099
Max sighed again. "Okay, I'll talk to my dad. But he won't like what I have to say."

